speechtext:
Section 258 of the Railway Act, not touched by this bill, reads as follows:
The board shall, without limiting any general power elsewhere conferred, have power, for the purpose of diminishing the danger at any highway crossing with any railway heretofore or hereafter constructed, to order
(a)	that any trees, buildings, earth or other obstruction to the view, which may be upon the railway, or the highway or any trees on any adjoining lands, shall be removed;
(b)	that nothing obstructing the view shall be placed at such crossing or nearer thereto than the board designates;
and for any such purpose the board shall have power to authorize or direct the expropriation of any land, the acquirement of any easement and the doing of anything deemed necessary, and shall have power to fix and order payment of such compensation as it deems just.
It would appear that the board has power to deal with obstruction of view either on the railway or the highway.
